==Description==

This BIP assigns flag byte 0x02 under Tapscript leaf version 0xc2 ([0xc2 BIP]) to the Schnorr signature scheme specified in [https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/blob/master/bip-0340.mediawiki BIP 340]. BIP 340 is the definitive specification for this scheme; this document defines only its integration into 0xc2 script semantics.

==Flag Byte==

0x02

==Parameters==

As specified in BIP 340.

==Key Format==

<code>pubkey_data</code> MUST be a 32-byte BIP 340 x-only public key. Any other size is an invalid encoding for this scheme.

==Signature Format==

As in BIP 342:

* 64 bytes: a BIP 340 signature, ''hash_type'' = 0x00 (SIGHASH_DEFAULT).
* 65 bytes: a BIP 340 signature followed by a ''hash_type'' byte, which MUST be valid per BIP 341 and MUST NOT be 0x00.
* Any other non-zero length is invalid.

==Verification Procedure==

Given a non-empty ''signature'' and ''pubkey_data'':

# If ''pubkey_data'' is not 32 bytes, fail.
# If ''signature'' is not 64 or 65 bytes, fail.
# If 65 bytes: let ''hash_type'' be the final byte; fail if 0x00 or invalid per BIP 341. Otherwise ''hash_type'' = 0x00.
# Compute the signature message per BIP 341 with the BIP 342 Tapscript extension, using ''key_version'' = 0xFF. Fail if the message cannot be computed.
# Apply BIP 340 ''Verify'' to the first 64 bytes of ''signature'', ''pubkey_data'', and the message. Fail on failure; otherwise succeed.

==Sigops Cost==

50 units per verification — identical to leaf version 0xc0, since verification is unchanged from BIP 340/342. This is the baseline against which future scheme BIPs scale their costs.

==Other Properties==

As documented in BIP 340: non-malleable, batch-verifiable, compatible with key/signature aggregation (e.g. MuSig2, BIP 327) and adaptor signatures. The flag byte exists only in script and affects none of these. No post-quantum security.

==Test Vectors==

BIP 340 ''Verify'' test vectors apply unchanged to step 5. Integration-level vectors (flag parsing, key/signature size checks, ''key_version'' 0xFF): [TBD] pending parent BIP finalization.

